Error [E1301]: `flag` expects 2 arguments (name, help), got 1
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_flag_arity.jet:4:25
    |
  4 |     spec #= args.spec().flag("verbose")
    |                         ^^^^
 Why: `ArgsSpec.flag(name, help)` registers a boolean flag like `--verbose`
 Fix: pass exactly two strings: the flag name and a help description

Error [E0108]: argument 1 to `.parse()` should be String (text), not [String]
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_flag_arity.jet:5:29
    |
  5 |     parsed #= spec.parse(io.args()) ?? panic("parse failed")
    |                             ^^^^
 Why: built-in methods need arguments of the right type
 Fix: put the value in text with interpolation: "{x}"

Error [E0311]: `flag` isn't a method on this value
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_flag_arity.jet:6:18
    |
  6 |     print(parsed.flag("verbose"))
    |                  ^^^^
 Why: only struct and enum values have instance methods
 Fix: check the spelling of `flag`
